  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Signs interpolate away: plain Pfaffian triple systems are #P-hard to count",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Counting the proper 2-colourings of 3-regular 3-uniform hypergraphs whose incidence graphs are Pfaffian is #P-hard under polynomial-time Turing reductions. A negated incidence is replaced by an unsigned long edge with k capped pairs, acting by 9^k (P+ + t P-) with t = (-1/3)^k; with L such edges the count is 9^(kL) q(t), deg q <= L, and q(-1) is the signed count (q(1) the count with the signs dropped). Long edges and caps inside planar pieces keep the Pfaffian certificate of SOFT-CROSS A, so composing with SOFT-CROSS B (Theorem 4) gives the theorem. Switching inside the pages leaves the soft crossing with 6 negations. Demonstrated end to end: 9 #col(K3,3) recovered from counts of plain Pfaffian instances only (k_S = 1, 3, 5, 7; 100 plain counts).",
  "dependencies": [
    "SOFT-CROSS-20261031-001B"
  ],
